  "doc": {
    "controller": "Every binding is a double-quoted value: QSettings reads an unquoted value with commas as a string list, which Azahar sees as empty and replaces with its keyboard default. Every binding reads the SDL game-controller API (api:controller) from whichever pad is present (maptype:all), with Azahar's own xinput_to_3ds_mapping numbers: Nintendo face buttons cross the Steam/Xbox labels deliberately, Start 6, Select 4, the d-pad 11-14, triggers are axes 4/5, and both analog sticks map to Circle Pad/C-Stick. In Game Mode that pad is Steam's virtual gamepad, the only one Steam lets a game see. Each key carries \\default=false, or a default Azahar saved earlier wins over the value.",
    "identity": "${controller_guid} comes from the target's input.json device_identities.azahar_controller_guid and is kept in each binding for reference; with maptype:all Azahar does not match it. It is the SDL GUID string as SDL 2.26+ prints it, with the name CRC in bytes 2-3 (Steam's virtual pad, Microsoft X-Box 360 pad 0, is 030079f6de280000ff11000001000000, as ES-DE logs it on the Deck). AzaharEmitter validates the 32-hex GUID and emits nothing when it is absent or malformed.",
    "touch": "Azahar's emu_window touch device consumes ABI-native bottom-screen coordinates from Semu surface 1. The source patch captures only successful presses and clamps captured movement; Steam Input routes the Deck's right trackpad as the pointer source. Motion remains Azahar's explicit motion emulator until the target declares and verifies a DSU motion source.",
    "storage": "Custom storage is disabled so NAND, SDMC saves, and save states remain below the isolated XDG data root. External aes_keys.txt and seeddb.bin sources are copied once into that root by emulator.json seeds.",
    "hotkeys": "Azahar reads its hotkeys only from [UI] as Shortcuts\\<group>\\<name>\\KeySeq (config.cpp:747-768, inside ReadUIValues), so the keymap rows and the blanks live in [UI]; each carries KeySeq\\default=false, or a default Azahar saved earlier wins. Chords are Qt portable text, the main Enter key spelled Return (Qt's Enter is the keypad key); a value with a comma is quoted (quote_commas), or QSettings reads it as an empty list. native_default_blanks writes every Azahar default whose key sequence is a Semu chord empty unless it is one of Semu's rows here: Audio Mute (Ctrl+M, the Semu menu), the 3D factor (Ctrl+- and Ctrl++), Multiplayer Browse Public Rooms (Ctrl+B), Toggle Frame Advancing (Ctrl+A), Toggle Status Bar (Ctrl+S), Exit Fullscreen (Esc) and, on Linux where the supervisor quits, Exit Azahar (Ctrl+Q). Qt fires neither of two shortcuts that share a sequence, so a leftover default would also silence Semu's own row. Swap Screens, Toggle Screen Layout and Rotate Screens Upright are always empty: SemuCompose re-derives Azahar's layout (semu_compose.btrc), so any of them would break the composed picture and touch. Quit is Semu's on Linux (the supervisor stops the process group), so Exit Azahar is bound only on macOS, whose supervisor reads no keyboard."
  },
  "native_shortcuts": {
    "source": "azahar fbd3fb0 src/citra_qt/configuration/config.cpp:59-102 (QtConfig::default_hotkeys, all in Main Window)",
    "fallback": true,
    "why": "ReadShortcutValues (config.cpp:747-768) reads [UI] Shortcuts\\<group>\\<name>\\KeySeq with ReadSetting(name, default): a shortcut the file leaves out keeps its default, so every default that shares a Semu chord is written empty. The settings are spelled as Azahar writes them, a / in a name becoming a group separator (Continue\\Pause%20Emulation).",
